# Adaptive Framework (AFW)

Metadata-driven **C** runtime (`libafw`) plus Python **`afwdev`**. Define functions, data types, object types, and interfaces in `generate/`; codegen fills `generated/`.

## Hard rules
- **"Get it right at most once"**: Humans edit only under `src/<srcdir>/generate/` (JSON/XML for metadata, `interfaces/*.xml`, `strings/`, EBNF comments, manifest stubs, etc.). The generator produces everything else. Never hand-edit **`generated/`** — `afwdev generate` deletes and rebuilds it.
- After metadata/C/afwdev changes, use the C-dev build below before trusting tests.
- Prefer existing patterns; match naming in `src/afw/doc/guide/developer/contributing.xml`.
- Primary agent focus: **C + Python (afwdev)**. JS/admin app only when explicitly asked.

## Layout
- `src/afw` — `libafw` (values, pools, xctx, compile/evaluate)
- `src/afw_dev` — `afwdev` CLI
- `src/afw_command` — `afw` CLI
- `src/afw_*` — extensions (same generate/generated pattern)
- `afw-package.json` — srcdirs / buildType / prefix

## Access model (short)
- Core, extensions, and commands interact through **interfaces** (XML under `generate/interfaces/` → generated headers/vtables).
- The primary integration point is the **shared environment** (`afw_environment_t` via `xctx->env`): almost every capability is a keyed entry in one of its registries (functions, data types, adapter types, content types, request handlers, etc.). Core registers at `AFW_ENVIRONMENT_CREATE` time; extensions and hosts (`afw`, `afwfcgi`) register later—often lazily via manifests. After registration they are peers under the same lookup APIs. See `afw-environment`.
- Core also owns the **script compiler + runtime** (`compile/`, `value/`, `xctx/`, `function/`). The compiler and expression lowering depend on functions already being registered (bootstrap order matters—see `afw-environment`). Grammar fragments are harvested from `/*ebnf>>> … <<<ebnf*/` comments in the parser sources—see `afw-compiler-ebnf`.

## Commands (package root)
```bash
# C/Python day-to-day: generate + cmake + install core/extensions/afwdev (not JS/docs)
./afwdev build --cdev -j

# Script tests (use installed afwdev after --cdev)
afwdev test -j

# Occasional memory check (much slower): before major PRs or memory work
afwdev test --env-mode valgrind -j

# Full repo including app + docs
./afwdev build --all --install -j

afwdev validate --pattern 'src/afw/generate/objects/...'
```

Use **`./afwdev`** when the build may refresh the installed `afwdev` itself; otherwise **`afwdev`** from PATH is fine.

